WEBVTT

00:15.260 --> 00:21.040
<i>We left this town, deep in the mountains, to look at the sea in the morning.</i>

00:21.040 --> 00:23.120
<i>Just me, Cynthia, and her bike.</i>

00:24.030 --> 00:26.900
<i>That experience was a first for me,</i>

00:26.900 --> 00:34.090
<i>but as I gazed at the sea, I was hit by a wave of nostalgia.</i>

00:34.510 --> 00:35.540
<i>How strange!</i>

00:47.500 --> 00:51.920
komorebi no mukougawa de

00:47.500 --> 00:51.920
Behind the veil of sunshine

00:52.280 --> 00:56.530
kimi wa mada kizuitenai no

00:52.280 --> 00:56.530
You have yet to realize

00:58.550 --> 01:00.900
watashi no koto

00:58.550 --> 01:00.900
That I'm here

01:00.900 --> 01:05.500
karuku te wo futte aizu shite

01:00.900 --> 01:05.500
I wave at you to say hi

01:06.460 --> 01:13.400
kakeyoru dake de ureshiku naru yo

01:06.460 --> 01:13.400
Just running up to you makes me happy

01:13.400 --> 01:20.180
kono mama de iraretara ii na

01:13.400 --> 01:20.180
I wish we could stay like this

01:20.470 --> 01:25.850
itsumo no sakamichi mo chotto

01:20.470 --> 01:25.850
I'd be so lonely on our usual slope

01:26.130 --> 01:28.960
setsunai no

01:26.130 --> 01:28.960
Otherwise

01:29.520 --> 01:36.940
kirisugita kami ga kaze ni yureru tabi

01:29.520 --> 01:36.940
I cut my hair too short, but the wind still catches it

01:36.940 --> 01:42.960
hanikamu yokogao kakushiteru no

01:36.940 --> 01:42.960
Hiding my blushing face

01:42.960 --> 01:50.170
taisetsuna ima wo tsumikasanete ikou

01:42.960 --> 01:50.170
Let's pile up all these precious moments

01:50.170 --> 01:53.900
mayou hi mo tanoshii hi mo

01:50.170 --> 01:53.900
All the bad days and the fun days

01:53.900 --> 01:58.930
takaramono ni naru kara

01:53.900 --> 01:58.930
Will become treasures in the future

02:12.450 --> 02:14.860
Would you listen to the rest of my song?

02:15.270 --> 02:17.820
Could you tell me more about Australia?

02:17.820 --> 02:21.780
I wanna ride behind you on your CBR and go somewhere!

02:21.780 --> 02:23.340
Cynthia-san!

02:23.340 --> 02:25.480
Whoa, okay!

02:25.480 --> 02:28.040
I'll grant all your wishes!

02:28.370 --> 02:31.460
Not so fast! Did you forget that we'll be busy, starting today?

02:31.460 --> 02:32.960
Oh, that <i>was— is</i> right!

02:34.470 --> 02:35.560
Starting today?

02:36.050 --> 02:37.420
What's happening?

02:37.970 --> 02:41.140
A group of astronomy enthusiasts are coming over.

02:41.140 --> 02:44.180
The skies are clear, so they'll have a great view!

02:45.270 --> 02:49.000
They can see the stars whenever they want. Why come now?

02:49.000 --> 02:50.690
Is it a large group?

02:50.690 --> 02:54.220
Yeah. We're fully booked for tomorrow.

02:54.220 --> 02:57.060
Despite that, those guests won't be using their beds!

02:57.060 --> 02:57.860
And that's because...

02:59.210 --> 03:01.460
They're all gonna go stargazing!

03:01.460 --> 03:03.370
Yeah! That's right!

03:05.390 --> 03:06.800
I wanna join in!

03:10.130 --> 03:14.060
A guest from last year sent us this picture.

03:16.490 --> 03:18.560
It's so pretty!

03:18.560 --> 03:21.320
I didn't know stars could look like that.

03:21.320 --> 03:23.160
Doesn't it look incredible, Maro?

03:24.790 --> 03:28.850
Stars actually come in many colors and shapes.

03:32.050 --> 03:33.310
<i>They're so pretty.</i>

03:34.550 --> 03:38.540
<i>Where are these colors hiding in the dark night sky?</i>

03:39.770 --> 03:43.740
<i>Could I see them too?</i>

03:43.740 --> 03:47.800
All right! I won't let you down, Papa-san!

03:47.800 --> 03:48.620
We're counting on you.

03:48.620 --> 03:51.680
I'll help too! Consider me a volunteer!

03:51.680 --> 03:53.220
Are you serious, Rie?

03:53.220 --> 03:54.750
Very serious!

03:55.850 --> 03:56.900
Sure you don't mind?

03:57.490 --> 03:59.000
I'll lend a hand too.

03:59.000 --> 04:00.720
Me too!

04:01.110 --> 04:03.840
Then come over tomorrow night.

04:05.130 --> 04:07.680
Ask your parents for permission when you get home, okay?

04:07.680 --> 04:08.500
Okay!

04:08.500 --> 04:10.820
This is great!

04:10.820 --> 04:12.310
Happiness squared!

04:14.290 --> 04:16.820
The first batch of guests are pulling in.

04:17.570 --> 04:19.020
Welcome!

04:19.610 --> 04:21.530
We're back.

04:21.530 --> 04:24.080
Nice to meet you!

04:24.080 --> 04:25.620
Welcome to Niwa Bed and Breakfast!

04:25.990 --> 04:27.480
Is she new?

04:27.480 --> 04:30.250
Yes! Nice to meet you!

04:30.250 --> 04:33.820
I want her to pay attention to me, not the guests!

04:33.820 --> 04:35.040
Why don't you stay over, then?

04:36.230 --> 04:39.300
A-chan, can I listen to the rest of the song?

04:40.250 --> 04:42.510
Why? Are you going to sing it?

04:42.510 --> 04:45.380
Yeah, I thought I'd give it a try.

04:44.190 --> 04:46.160
Haruno-senpai!

04:46.160 --> 04:49.220
Finally decided to make your world debut, huh?

04:49.220 --> 04:50.940
No, that's not it.

04:50.940 --> 04:53.320
You are <i>too</i> cute!

04:53.320 --> 04:55.020
Just one second.

04:55.710 --> 04:59.100
I wonder if that trip to the sea with Cynthia-san changed her.

04:59.100 --> 05:02.360
Whatever changed her, it got her to sing for me! Here!

05:02.750 --> 05:05.500
I can't promise that I'll be able to sing it well though.

05:05.500 --> 05:07.740
You'll do fine!

05:27.790 --> 05:29.660
She's reacting better than usual.

05:29.660 --> 05:31.260
She sure is.

05:31.260 --> 05:33.830
Hey, did you finish the lyrics yet?

05:33.830 --> 05:36.690
Actually, I've been having trouble with that part.

05:38.130 --> 05:40.060
Then Sayo-senpai can write
the lyrics instead, right?

05:42.810 --> 05:43.990
Poetry...

05:49.970 --> 05:51.520
I think we can take that as a yes!

05:51.520 --> 05:56.740
All right! Now your team is complete!

05:56.740 --> 05:57.740
Team?

05:57.740 --> 05:58.870
Yeah!

05:58.870 --> 06:02.320
A band made up of real high school girls!

06:02.320 --> 06:03.760
A band, huh?

06:03.760 --> 06:05.420
Sounds like fun.

06:05.420 --> 06:06.510
Yeah, I guess.

06:07.110 --> 06:08.360
What's going on?

06:07.110 --> 06:08.900
Hurray!

06:08.360 --> 06:10.300
Is it the Cynthia-effect?

06:10.300 --> 06:12.220
I believe so.

06:13.570 --> 06:15.670
You should name your band "Doggy"!

06:15.670 --> 06:16.840
Forget it.

06:23.270 --> 06:25.240
Just put them wherever.

06:25.240 --> 06:27.860
Okay! This is easy as cake!

06:27.860 --> 06:29.780
I think you mean "easy as pie."

06:29.780 --> 06:31.030
Oh, sorry.

06:31.870 --> 06:34.340
I'm looking forward to hearing your band.

06:34.340 --> 06:35.460
Really?

06:35.460 --> 06:37.700
Yeah, I can't wait to hear you sing!

06:38.830 --> 06:40.800
When's the concert?

06:43.270 --> 06:44.880
Concert?

06:44.880 --> 06:49.400
Yeah! You've gotta perform at a concert when your song's done!

06:49.840 --> 06:51.680
Haruno! Yeah, yeah!

06:50.910 --> 06:52.840
A concert...

06:51.680 --> 06:53.040
Anri! Whoa!

06:53.040 --> 06:54.580
Sayocchi! Rwoar!

06:57.270 --> 06:59.920
Thanks for coming to see us perform!

07:00.900 --> 07:04.360
Please listen to our new song!

07:05.430 --> 07:07.820
It's titled... "Untitled"!

07:07.820 --> 07:12.560
<i>I live on a mountain.</i>

07:16.070 --> 07:21.170
<i>We've got lots of chickens there.</i>

07:21.170 --> 07:23.460
Oh yeah!

07:24.700 --> 07:29.460
Anri! Sayocchi! Riecchi! Twang, twang!

07:27.950 --> 07:29.460
We're not having a concert.

07:30.670 --> 07:31.980
Why not?

07:32.790 --> 07:35.640
We're not good enough to perform at one.

07:36.030 --> 07:38.840
No problem! All you have to do is practice!

07:39.510 --> 07:41.680
It's not as easy as you think.

07:42.270 --> 07:44.540
Concert!

07:44.540 --> 07:45.420
Are you having one?

07:45.420 --> 07:46.480
Nope.

07:46.480 --> 07:48.000
Concert!

07:48.000 --> 07:49.440
Answer's still no.

07:49.930 --> 07:51.080
Concert!

07:51.080 --> 07:52.150
I said no!

07:52.150 --> 07:53.050
Conc—

07:53.050 --> 07:53.860
We can't!

08:04.850 --> 08:06.320
We can do it!

08:08.510 --> 08:10.380
We can go wherever we want!

08:10.380 --> 08:13.050
Even Africa or the South Pole?

08:13.050 --> 08:15.050
You bet!

08:15.050 --> 08:16.720
Even Dad said so!

08:17.030 --> 08:18.080
But...

08:18.080 --> 08:19.860
It's true!

08:19.860 --> 08:22.180
It'd be cool if we could really do that.

08:23.550 --> 08:26.840
We should travel around the world together!

08:26.840 --> 08:29.020
All of us? Together?

08:29.350 --> 08:31.640
Yup! All together!

08:35.930 --> 08:38.870
I'm having second thoughts about this.

08:39.590 --> 08:40.720
What about you, Sayocchi?

08:40.720 --> 08:41.980
Likewise.

08:41.980 --> 08:47.020
You guys'll be fine! I bet they'll even invite you to sing on that annual music show, <i>Kouhaku</i>!

08:47.020 --> 08:47.960
<i>Kouhaku</i>?!

08:47.960 --> 08:50.340
Before you know it,
you'll be taking the whole world by storm!

08:50.340 --> 08:51.740
Oh, please!

08:51.740 --> 08:52.860
Like that could happen!

08:54.190 --> 08:57.620
Cynthia-san's probably rolling in her grave.

08:57.620 --> 08:58.890
She's not dead!

09:00.250 --> 09:02.350
Think before you speak, would you?

09:02.710 --> 09:03.960
Still...

09:04.700 --> 09:06.350
I think we should give it a try!

09:06.850 --> 09:07.600
What?

09:07.600 --> 09:09.930
See? Haruno-senpai's a real go-getter!

09:09.930 --> 09:11.140
Aim for no less than <i>Kouhaku</i>!

09:11.140 --> 09:12.360
I wasn't talking about that.

09:13.190 --> 09:14.660
I was talking about a concert.

09:15.470 --> 09:17.070
We should give it a try.

09:17.510 --> 09:19.840
A concert? Why?

09:20.450 --> 09:21.910
Well...

09:21.910 --> 09:25.400
We've got some songs we made a while back and...

09:25.870 --> 09:29.580
I just wanna do something with all of you.

09:31.130 --> 09:32.860
Does that include me too?

09:32.860 --> 09:34.340
Yeah. All three of you guys.

09:35.610 --> 09:36.800
How about it?

09:44.290 --> 09:47.920
<i>I remember feeling this way when we were kids.</i>

09:48.810 --> 09:52.420
<i>I kept running ahead, but they would hesitate to follow.</i>

09:53.070 --> 09:56.640
<i>That's why I decided not to go overboard.</i>

09:57.690 --> 10:00.070
Sorry. Forget I said anything.

10:05.850 --> 10:09.000
<i>I shouldn't have brought the concert up.</i>

10:09.730 --> 10:14.680
<i>Being with them tonight is going to be so awkward.</i>

10:29.650 --> 10:30.860
Hello!

10:32.310 --> 10:34.260
Oh, welcome!

10:34.260 --> 10:36.360
Welcome!

10:37.870 --> 10:39.740
I've got a reservation under the name Kageyama.

10:54.320 --> 10:57.240
I'll bring them the boar stew!

10:57.240 --> 10:58.010
Thanks!

10:58.670 --> 10:59.880
Which one would you like?

10:59.880 --> 11:01.320
Um...

11:01.320 --> 11:02.580
Good evening!

11:02.580 --> 11:03.980
Here they are!

11:03.980 --> 11:04.970
Good evening to you too.

11:04.970 --> 11:07.930
Um, have you seen Haruno?

11:11.210 --> 11:12.940
Would you like some coffee?

11:12.940 --> 11:14.320
Oh, I'd love some.

11:15.050 --> 11:17.230
I like this place.

11:17.230 --> 11:18.820
That's good to hear.

11:22.150 --> 11:24.620
Is that a telescope?

11:24.620 --> 11:26.230
Oh, this?

11:26.230 --> 11:28.220
Yeah, it's a Dobsonian telescope.

11:28.220 --> 11:29.620
I'll let you have a look.

11:29.620 --> 11:30.660
Really?

11:37.390 --> 11:40.900
Were you expecting to see a starry sky like the ones in photos?

11:40.900 --> 11:43.200
Yes. Do you use something different for that?

11:43.200 --> 11:47.060
Those photos are a product of long-exposure photography.

11:47.630 --> 11:50.020
You need the long exposure time to get them to look like that.

11:50.570 --> 11:52.120
Don't you think it's marvelous?

11:52.120 --> 11:54.560
So you aren't taking pictures?

11:54.560 --> 11:59.810
I just watch them like this or through my telescope sometimes.

11:59.810 --> 12:00.780
Nothing more.

12:01.650 --> 12:05.450
I love watching them and getting lost in thought.

12:08.400 --> 12:14.160
Is the night sky full of stars that are as beautiful as flowers?

12:14.160 --> 12:15.260
Yeah.

12:15.260 --> 12:17.520
They're too far away to see clearly,

12:17.520 --> 12:20.520
but if you give it enough time, you'll be able to see them.

12:21.530 --> 12:24.580
The same thing applies to a person's heart.

12:25.270 --> 12:27.360
<i>A person's heart...</i>

12:29.150 --> 12:36.080
<i>Maybe I should put some more time into considering how others feel.</i>

12:37.390 --> 12:39.020
Kage-chan!

12:39.020 --> 12:40.860
Getting lost in thought again?

12:41.450 --> 12:44.600
With all my might, Cynthia!

12:45.140 --> 12:46.530
You two sure hit it off quick.

12:48.740 --> 12:51.580
I brought you some boar stew.

12:52.690 --> 12:56.560
You came to help after all! Thanks!

12:58.710 --> 13:01.200
Just forget about what I said earlier, okay?

13:01.200 --> 13:03.920
I don't know what came over me. Sorry.

13:05.430 --> 13:08.680
Um, if we were to have a concert, where would it be?

13:10.640 --> 13:14.060
I wasn't really paying attention.

13:14.060 --> 13:16.840
Did you want to perform at the Budokan arena?

13:16.840 --> 13:18.180
Of course not!

13:18.180 --> 13:21.520
The small stage at our inn would be fine.

13:21.520 --> 13:22.610
Oh!

13:23.050 --> 13:25.380
How does Poco a Poco sound?

13:26.370 --> 13:28.340
For our band's name!

13:28.340 --> 13:30.780
It means "little by little."

13:32.810 --> 13:33.900
Uh...

13:34.790 --> 13:36.250
I like it!

13:37.870 --> 13:40.220
Okay! Now let's go help out!

13:40.220 --> 13:41.210
Yup!

13:42.890 --> 13:48.900
<i>It turns out that the mountain I thought I could never overcome wasn't so big after all.</i>

13:49.590 --> 13:53.840
<i>We all could go a bit further together!</i>

13:54.530 --> 13:57.620
<i>Step by step, little by little.</i>

14:15.850 --> 14:18.360
We're going in, Kage-chan.

14:18.360 --> 14:19.240
Okay.

14:28.090 --> 14:30.680
We came for your eggs.

14:33.730 --> 14:39.730
Kageyama-san stayed after the stargazing event ended and the other guests left.

14:40.730 --> 14:46.530
4th Road
New memories begin

14:41.250 --> 14:42.800
She's been there ever since?

14:42.800 --> 14:45.220
Yeah. She and Cynthia are like best friends now.

14:45.220 --> 14:46.690
Doesn't she have a job?

14:46.690 --> 14:51.300
She said she writes children's books, so she has a lot of free time.

14:51.300 --> 14:52.700
So she's a writer.

14:52.700 --> 14:53.680
Yup.

14:54.660 --> 14:58.840
Come to think of it, she does have a certain style or aura about her.

15:01.420 --> 15:03.880
Poco! A! Poco!

15:04.350 --> 15:05.520
What was that supposed to be?

15:05.520 --> 15:08.340
A greeting! What else?!

15:08.340 --> 15:11.600
By the way, have you finished the lyrics yet, Sayo-senpai?

15:11.600 --> 15:12.360
Nope.

15:12.360 --> 15:14.280
Anri-senpai, any progress on the song?

15:14.280 --> 15:16.220
I'm still not done.

15:16.220 --> 15:18.640
Haruno-senpai, have you been practicing singing?

15:18.640 --> 15:20.310
Not... really.

15:20.310 --> 15:23.800
You guys need to take this seriously!

15:23.800 --> 15:26.520
Be aware of your duties as band members!

15:26.520 --> 15:28.280
I...

15:28.280 --> 15:29.900
Uh...

15:33.290 --> 15:35.380
I've got nothing to do!

15:35.380 --> 15:36.820
That's true.

15:38.370 --> 15:41.500
It's okay! We need you, Riecchi!

15:41.500 --> 15:42.740
Do you really?

15:42.740 --> 15:44.250
Um...

15:45.610 --> 15:46.880
You could be our manager!

15:47.620 --> 15:50.560
Your... manager?

15:51.760 --> 15:53.260
And our backup singer!

15:53.730 --> 15:55.280
We need a tambourine player too!

15:56.310 --> 15:58.180
Poco a Poco!

16:01.330 --> 16:03.620
We're expecting a lot from you, Riecchi.

16:04.610 --> 16:08.820
Okay! Follow your manager Rie!

16:09.130 --> 16:10.320
Let's do our best!

16:10.320 --> 16:11.380
Yeah!

16:11.380 --> 16:13.000
Poco a Poco!

16:13.000 --> 16:14.780
Talk about quick mood swings...

16:15.410 --> 16:18.660
Let's have a meeting at Motoya after school!

16:18.660 --> 16:19.960
Okay.

16:27.130 --> 16:30.140
Look alive, you guys! It's time to start out meeting!

16:30.140 --> 16:30.960
Okay.

16:32.330 --> 16:34.220
Would you guys take this seriously?!

16:34.220 --> 16:35.740
We <i>are</i>!

16:35.740 --> 16:38.220
In fact, I can hear a melody ringing in my ear right now!

16:38.220 --> 16:41.430
A great phrase... is just a bit of inspiration away!

16:41.850 --> 16:44.310
I'm doing mental training!

16:47.180 --> 16:50.020
Have we even decided when we're having the concert?

16:50.730 --> 16:52.140
What's a good time?

16:52.140 --> 16:54.360
How about next spring?

16:54.360 --> 16:55.920
Sounds good to me.

16:55.920 --> 16:58.500
We should prepare as best we can.

16:59.530 --> 17:00.790
Spring, huh?

17:00.790 --> 17:03.720
I wonder if I'll be able to get my driver's license before then.

17:18.350 --> 17:20.390
Whoa, he fixed it?

17:20.390 --> 17:23.400
I thought he said it was missing a part.

17:23.400 --> 17:25.920
He must've made a replacement.

17:25.920 --> 17:27.480
What amazing determination!

17:27.480 --> 17:28.360
We can all learn something from him!

17:28.360 --> 17:34.820
That's the sound of many parts working together.

17:36.990 --> 17:38.840
Like a good band!

17:39.280 --> 17:42.460
The parts work together to create music.

17:42.460 --> 17:43.880
That's what a true band does.

17:43.880 --> 17:47.240
We should rev up our engine too!

17:47.240 --> 17:50.480
Damn, I just said something really cool, didn't I?!

17:50.480 --> 17:52.400
Am I awesome or what?!

17:52.400 --> 17:55.420
Come on, don't be shy! Tell me how awesome I am—

17:55.420 --> 17:56.630
Get back here!

17:57.210 --> 17:59.160
Wow, you're so awesome, Riecchi.

17:59.160 --> 18:02.720
Don't be mean! Say it like you mean it!

18:17.810 --> 18:20.450
No way! Cynthia really said that?

18:20.450 --> 18:25.360
Yeah. She's just helping out "for a while."

18:32.770 --> 18:34.340
I'm sure we'll all miss her.

18:35.730 --> 18:37.420
I'll be okay!

18:38.470 --> 18:41.120
I'm not sure how the others will react though.

18:44.330 --> 18:46.480
I'm home!

18:46.480 --> 18:48.520
Shopping mission complete!

18:48.520 --> 18:51.620
How's that new dessert you're working on? Will it be tasty?

18:53.230 --> 18:54.940
I sure hope so.

18:58.030 --> 18:59.450
Haruno?

18:59.850 --> 19:03.200
Cynthia, are you quitting?

19:03.950 --> 19:07.250
Yeah. I've been meaning to tell you.

19:07.690 --> 19:10.710
We decided to have our concert next spring.

19:12.770 --> 19:16.760
I'm leaving next Saturday.

19:19.590 --> 19:20.720
I see.

19:29.770 --> 19:33.000
Does this mean I won't get to hear your songs?

19:34.250 --> 19:35.750
I don't know.

19:35.750 --> 19:37.860
I'll ask the others.

19:53.850 --> 19:55.420
I don't get it.

19:59.750 --> 20:01.380
I knew she'd come.

20:02.650 --> 20:04.420
This spot has a great view.

20:05.910 --> 20:08.140
Kageyama-san? What're you doing here?

20:08.670 --> 20:12.100
Cynthia told me about this spot. Mind if I sit with you?

20:12.100 --> 20:14.400
Not at all. Go right ahead.

20:16.310 --> 20:18.580
Seriously, the view from here is great.

20:18.580 --> 20:21.280
I'll make some tea.

20:22.270 --> 20:22.990
Thanks.

20:23.770 --> 20:27.080
Cynthia's going home to Australia.

20:27.910 --> 20:30.620
She can't put it off.

20:31.960 --> 20:33.620
I see.

20:36.030 --> 20:39.660
It's pretty amazing how she's traveled all around the world.

20:40.210 --> 20:44.980
She says she'll stay put for a while once she gets to Australia.

20:46.030 --> 20:49.120
Cynthia may seem carefree, but even she has responsibilities.

20:51.670 --> 20:54.830
She's not visiting anywhere in Japan after this, right?

20:54.830 --> 20:56.060
It would seem so.

20:56.060 --> 20:59.820
Then she should've visited places more interesting than here.

21:00.630 --> 21:05.940
I guess Mom asked her to stay and inspire me, but still...

21:05.940 --> 21:08.500
I think Cynthia wanted to stay here.

21:08.500 --> 21:10.060
Oh really?

21:10.690 --> 21:13.440
She probably wanted to encourage you.

21:15.290 --> 21:16.410
Thanks.

21:16.410 --> 21:18.650
Encourage, huh?

21:18.650 --> 21:23.700
She told me I should rely on people more,

21:23.700 --> 21:27.920
but I'm not sure what I want to do is worth the effort.

21:27.920 --> 21:29.980
You mean singing?

21:29.980 --> 21:32.600
I'm not even sure if singing <i>is</i> what I want to do.

21:33.770 --> 21:35.410
I don't see the problem.

21:35.410 --> 21:36.560
That's how life is sometimes.

21:37.510 --> 21:41.280
How can I ask for encouragement
when I don't know what I want to do?

21:41.280 --> 21:44.840
You don't really ask people to encourage you.

21:45.710 --> 21:48.420
Someone will encourage you if they see you devoting yourself to something.

21:48.950 --> 21:51.800
The people being encouraged are often too busy working hard to notice.

21:51.800 --> 21:55.600
It's not a visible strength, but that doesn't mean it isn't important.

21:56.120 --> 21:59.130
Did you have someone to encourage you too, Kageyama-san?

21:59.130 --> 22:00.660
Of course!

22:01.270 --> 22:05.220
No one's ever achieved their dreams without being encouraged by someone else.

22:08.260 --> 22:11.720
I'd love to hear your song too!

22:17.950 --> 22:20.060
Cynthia-san!

22:21.310 --> 22:24.040
There, there. I know how you feel.

22:24.530 --> 22:25.940
What should we do?

22:26.870 --> 22:29.360
Your guess is as good as mine.

22:29.360 --> 22:31.400
Why are we hesitating?

22:32.230 --> 22:33.960
We've got to do it!

22:33.960 --> 22:36.220
We've got to complete the song by next week!

22:36.220 --> 22:38.290
Let's ask Cynthia-san for help!

22:38.290 --> 22:41.160
No! We can't rely on her for this!

22:42.610 --> 22:45.760
This is our way of thanking her.

22:45.760 --> 22:46.780
Yeah.

22:55.630 --> 22:57.140
Poco a Poco!

23:01.330 --> 23:04.570
<i>Our engine started up too.</i>

23:05.330 --> 23:08.070
<i>We decided to write a song about ourselves,</i>

23:08.490 --> 23:11.530
<i>and even though we were so excited about it during the meeting,</i>

23:11.530 --> 23:13.000
Thank you!

23:12.270 --> 23:16.620
<i>we had no idea where to start.</i>

23:17.200 --> 23:23.340
<i>We've been thinking about the song every moment since then.</i>

23:24.450 --> 23:27.420
<i>We did everything we could.</i>

23:29.970 --> 23:34.740
<i>We even listened to Cynthia's stories.</i>

23:34.740 --> 23:37.580
<i>And before long, our song started to take shape.</i>

23:39.910 --> 23:44.230
<i>Our paths may diverge one day, but...</i>

23:44.230 --> 23:47.800
<i>...I'm sure that ten, even twenty years from now,</i>

23:47.800 --> 23:50.920
<i>we'll remember these days and how we wrote this song.</i>

23:51.430 --> 23:53.740
<i>As well as how good this wind feels.</i>

23:54.820 --> 23:57.960
<i>A small and inconvenient town in the mountains.</i>

23:58.610 --> 24:00.160
<i>Chatting idly.</i>

24:00.930 --> 24:03.480
<i>That's all part of who we are!</i>

24:05.310 --> 24:08.000
<i>We'll make sure that you'll never forget us,</i>

24:08.000 --> 24:10.630
<i>no matter how far you go!</i>

24:12.830 --> 24:16.520
<i>We managed to complete the song with little time to spare.</i>

24:16.520 --> 24:19.360
<i>Our first performance is tomorrow!</i>

24:21.110 --> 24:22.780
I wonder if it'll be good.

24:22.780 --> 24:24.780
We won't know until we sing tomorrow.

24:25.850 --> 24:27.560
I'm sure she'll love it.

24:29.590 --> 24:31.640
Maro thinks so too!

